{"name":"Midnight Serenade","hex":"#41434e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"midnight","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The middle of the night: the sixth temporal hour, equidistant between sunset and sunrise.","Twelve o'clock at night exactly."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Utterly dark or black."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/midnight"},{"term":"serenade","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A love song that is sung directly to one's love interest, especially one performed below the window of a loved one in the evening.","An instrumental composition in several movements."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To sing or play a serenade for (someone).","To woo someone."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/serenade"}],"entries":[{"title":"Midnight","blocks":[{"text":"Midnight is the transition time from one day to the next – the moment when the date changes, on the local official clock time for any particular jurisdiction. By clock time, midnight is the opposite of noon, differing from it by 12 hours."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Tour_de_l%27horloge_de_la_gare_de_Metz_%C3%A0_Minuit_%28juin_2019%29_%28cropped%29.JPG/330px-Tour_de_l%27horloge_de_la_gare_de_Metz_%C3%A0_Minuit_%28juin_2019%29_%28cropped%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midnight","wikidata":"Q36402"},{"title":"Serenade","blocks":[{"text":"In music, a serenade is a musical composition or performance delivered in honour of someone or something. Serenades are typically calm, light pieces of music. The term comes from the Italian word serenata, which itself derives from the Latin serenus. The sense was influenced by Italian sera \"evening\", from Latin sera, fem. of serus \"late\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Judith_Leyster_Serenade.jpg/330px-Judith_Leyster_Serenade.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Serenade","wikidata":"Q215911"},{"title":"Midnight blue","blocks":[{"text":"Midnight blue is a dark shade of blue named for its resemblance to the apparently blue color of a moonlit night sky around a full moon. Midnight blue is identifiably blue to the eye in sunlight or full-spectrum light, but can appear black under certain more limited spectra sometimes found in artificial lighting. It is similar to navy, which is also a dark blue."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/D%C3%BCsseldorf_Midnight_view.jpg/330px-D%C3%BCsseldorf_Midnight_view.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midnight_blue","wikidata":"Q947638"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Midnight_Mist.jpg/500px-Midnight_Mist.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Midnight_Mist.jpg/500px-Midnight_Mist.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Photograph of the moon taken at midnight","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMidnight_Mist.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Serenade_in_the_Ottoman_Empire.jpg/500px-Serenade_in_the_Ottoman_Empire.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Serenade_in_the_Ottoman_Empire.jpg/1280px-Serenade_in_the_Ottoman_Empire.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Serenade_in_the_Ottoman_Empire.jpg/500px-Serenade_in_the_Ottoman_Empire.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Serenade in the Ottoman empire, 1688","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASerenade_in_the_Ottoman_Empire.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Nellie_Bly-6m-in-Mexico-14.jpg/250px-Nellie_Bly-6m-in-Mexico-14.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/be/Nellie_Bly-6m-in-Mexico-14.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Nellie_Bly-6m-in-Mexico-14.jpg/250px-Nellie_Bly-6m-in-Mexico-14.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A young woman being serenaded by a man in the street below","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANellie_Bly-6m-in-Mexico-14.jpg"}],"sounds":{"midnight":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/36/En-us-midnight.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/3/36/En-us-midnight.ogg/En-us-midnight.ogg.mp3"}],"serenade":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e2/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-serenade.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/e/e2/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-serenade.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-serenade.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/e/e2/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-serenade.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-serenade.wav.ogg"}]}}}